WEBVTT

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.650
<i>I've got a bad feeling.</i>

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.740
<i>And my hunches are usually spot-on.</i>

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:11.860
<i>I have no idea what's going to happen,</i>

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:13.080
Seriously?

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.940
<i>but today it feels particularly bad.</i>

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.250
<i>No...</i>

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.670
<i>It can't be something this simple.</i>

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.780
<i>Is there any way I can avoid this?</i>

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.750
<i>When I had this kind of feeling before, 
I tried to keep the trouble from happening...</i>

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.290
<i>But it didn't work, and bad 
luck found me anyway.</i>

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:41.900
<i>And this time, the bad feeling is even worse.</i>

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.320
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.300
<i>Is she seriously a model?</i>

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:43.600
Damn it!

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.980
When I close my eyes, I see her face...

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:50.810
I never should've looked at that magazine.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.980
I've never seen a model like that before.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:01.490
But could a fashion model who's
that creepy-looking actually exist?

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.950
Maybe it was just an unflattering picture.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.570
But Oda,

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:08.550
the memory of it has warped
so much in my head

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.450
that she just looks like a monster now!

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.100
Forget that, Iwasaki.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.500
Is the script coming along?

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.720
Nope, not at all.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:17.120
How are we gonna film 
a movie without a script?

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:19.120
I know it's just club stuff,
but don't slack so much.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.770
I wasn't trying to slack off!

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:24.170
Dude, don't tell me this model has you 
so freaked that you can't write.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:26.290
If you don't wanna do it,
I can ask someone else.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:28.380
We're submitting this one 
for a contest, after all.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.380
I know, I know.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.100
<i>I didn't have another
chance to see that model,</i>

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:52.300
<i>and for a while, I was just disturbed by my 
warped memory of her appearance...</i>

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:56.080
<i>But thankfully, as time passed,
those memories faded.</i>

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:57.710
The script was good!

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.020
No, it was your camera work, Oda.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:02.000
Don't get modest on me, Iwasaki!

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.040
Nah, it was my lighting!

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:08.660
Gotta say, I never even dreamed
we'd win the grand prize.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:09.970
"Dream" is the right word.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:13.570
But this means that as far as
amateur filmmakers go,

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:15.600
people are gonna know our names.

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:19.100
Which is why I wanted
to make a proposal...

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.700
How about an open audition for 
the heroine of our next film?

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:22.680
Why?

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.450
Couldn't we just find
someone from the school?

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:28.790
Nah, I don't know any girl in this school
who's pretty enough to star in our film.

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:30.130
If we open it up to the public,

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:31.950
we'll find someone with the right look.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.400
After all, we've got a reputation now!

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:38.000
Only three submissions, huh?

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:41.020
Guess our reputation
doesn't amount to much.

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:44.590
Not what I had in mind...

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:47.460
She's great!

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.050
She is!

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:50.470
She's the one!

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:52.740
Reputation is about <i>who</i> knows you,
not how many know you!

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:54.000
What's up, Miyake?

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.700
Just thinking about how cute she is...

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.350
It almost feels like a destined meeting.

00:04:57.610 --> 00:04:59.310
I forgot about this one...

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.450
What the hell?

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:08.340
Seriously, what is this?

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:09.460
Who's this supposed to be?

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:11.410
What is it, Iwasaki?

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.320
That's her! The model I mentioned!

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:15.360
This is her?

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:16.940
You sure you're not mistaken?

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:18.710
I'm positive!

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:20.520
Look at those creepy features!

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:24.420
Why would a professional model
audition for an amateur movie?

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:26.050
I know it's her!

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.880
Just seeing her again is giving me chills!

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:29.940
Okay, how about this?

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:31.680
We'll cast her in the movie, too.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.200
Along with the beauty.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.090
Are you serious?!

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:37.020
Cut the sick jokes, Oda!

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.950
Or do you want to turn
this into a horror movie?

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:40.500
Just hear me out.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:43.670
She's definitely creepy, 
but if you think about it,

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:46.320
I've never seen someone
with a look this unique.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:51.330
So, Mori Tamae-san,
you're a first-year in high school?

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:54.180
You're even cuter than your picture!

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:55.180
I wouldn't say that...

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:56.640
You're going to be our star!

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.620
You'll be playing the heroine.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:01.700
Don't worry about the acting. Just be natural.

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:02.290
Okay.

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:05.600
You really are cute...

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:06.290
Whoa!

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:11.760
I'm Fuchi.

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:15.120
O-Oh, Fuchi-san...

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:16.820
Have a seat.

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:19.510
Fuchi-san, you're a 
professional model, right?

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:21.480
This is Iwasaki.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.010
He's a fan of yours.

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:24.300
Oda!

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.900
Don't make up stuff about
how I'm that woman's fan!

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:36.130
Sorry, sorry.

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:39.210
Still, that is one creepy woman.

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:43.270
And I had no idea she would be so huge.

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:45.270
She's not gonna fit in the frame!

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:49.840
Can't you just get her off 
the project somehow, Oda?

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:52.040
Look, don't worry.

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:54.840
She was just nervous about 
meeting us for the first time.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:57.540
Depending on your perspective, 
she could be a real asset.

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.860
In terms of screen presence, 
she might eat our star up!

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:05.100
I definitely have a
bad feeling about this...

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.780
Hey, Oda, how much farther 
to the location for the shoot?

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.400
Almost there.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:19.040
Can we hurry this up? 
I feel like I'm suffocating.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.770
You'll have all the fresh air you
can breathe when we get there.

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:24.790
This is deep in the mountains,
far away from any people.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.250
It's a perfect fit for the script's setting!

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.010
Isolated deep in the mountains,
away from any people?

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:30.950
So it'll be a horror movie after all?

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:33.170
Don't be stupid.

00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:35.640
That was good!

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:54.890
Dude, did you see that?!

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:57.240
Yeah... Is she even human?

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:00.240
Those weren't teeth... They were fangs!

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:02.980
Well? Beautiful location, right?

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:04.170
Yes.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:09.720
I love places like this.

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:12.560
You wanna react as if the
audience is looking from over here.

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:13.700
So you turn around...

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:15.140
Now, the camera will be here,

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:17.610
so you want to give it a second
and then step forward suddenly.

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:18.310
Okay.

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:24.120
Hey, Iwasaki...

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:26.180
I think she's into you.

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:27.340
Dumbass!

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:28.980
Don't joke about that!

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.730
Where are you going, man?

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:35.570
I feel kind of sick,

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:37.610
so I'm gonna go wash
my face in the river.

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:19.240
Where have you been, Iwasaki?

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:22.120
You're playing opposite our 
heroine, so you can't just—

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.400
Is something wrong?

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:25.470
Where's that woman?

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:27.880
I couldn't care less where she is!

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:32.370
Look, let's get out of here
before she gets back.

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:33.620
What? Why?

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:35.840
I don't want to be around that freak!

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:38.540
So we just leave her here by herself?

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:40.090
Exactly!

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:42.180
Come on, what do you guys think?

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:46.030
But we're in the middle of the mountains...

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:46.760
Shh!

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.120
And cut!

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:57.050
Tamae-chan!

00:09:57.050 --> 00:09:59.670
You were great in that scene! Good job!

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:00.320
Thank you.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:01.540
Excuse me.

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:05.320
You've only been filming
her for a while now.

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:09.320
When are we going to 
be filming my scenes?

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.650
Oh, sorry about that!

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:15.000
Your role's a critical one, so why don't
you take a break before we start?

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:20.870
But if we leave her here, I'm afraid 
she'll come after us for revenge.

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:24.290
We should just film whatever and look
for a chance to say we're done with her.

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:25.480
Not me!

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:27.390
I say we run right now,
while she's not around!

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:31.030
Right now? Tamae-chan's 
on break, too, y'know.

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:33.090
Miyake's gone, too...

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.650
H-Hey! Trouble!

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:37.200
What is it, Miyake?

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.550
It's bad...

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:39.680
Calm down.

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:41.160
Catch your breath and tell us.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:42.330
What is it?

00:10:42.770 --> 00:10:45.180
In the mountains... Tamae-chan...

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:46.790
Fuchi's eating her!

00:10:48.190 --> 00:10:49.630
Fuchi!

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:52.510
The fashion model is eating Tamae-chan!

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:53.540
She was chewing her up!

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:55.540
What the hell are you talking about?

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:57.250
I'm serious!

00:10:57.250 --> 00:11:01.430
We were all fawning over 
Tamae-chan, so she ate her!

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.450
Miyake, your sense of humor is screwed up.

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:04.900
It's the truth, damn it!

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:07.080
If you don't believe me, then go look!

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:11.400
I don't wanna go back there.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:14.300
How are we gonna find them
if you don't show us the way?

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:16.320
I believe him.

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.240
I'd believe she could eat someone.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:21.240
Are you seriously buying into this, Iwasaki?

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:24.080
They were over there.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:27.610
I don't see anyone.

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:29.210
Look!

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:31.500
That's blood!

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:34.500
Look around! There are 
blood stains everywhere!

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:35.500
Then is it true?!

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:38.200
But where is she?

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.760
Now I'm the star.

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:48.850
Run!

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:50.680
Get back here!

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:55.890
Help!

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:56.610
Miyake!

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:04.450
Hey! Wait up!

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.000
<i>I've got a bad feeling...</i>

00:12:10.820 --> 00:12:13.420
<i>And my hunches are usually right...</i>

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:15.320
<i>Today's feels...</i>

00:12:15.890 --> 00:12:17.420
<i>particularly bad!</i>

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:23.010
We're finally alone...

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:28.010
<b>Fashion Model</b>

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:28.010
Collection No. 041

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:31.630
<i>I don't want to die.</i>

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:34.980
<i>But I'm going to die soon...</i>

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:37.240
<i>I'll be dead... I'll become nothing.</i>

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:39.490
<i>I'm going to stop existing...</i>

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:40.960
I'm scared!

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:42.900
I'm scared...

00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:46.420
I'm scared!

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:50.820
Who's there?

00:12:51.890 --> 00:12:53.000
Who are you?

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:04.130
No!

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:04.130
<b>General Hospital</b>

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:09.140
<b>Long Dreams</b>

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:09.140
Collection No. 084

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:11.100
<b>Neurosurgery Ward</b>

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:11.600
Doctor!

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.540
I don't want to die!

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:15.090
I don't want to become nothing!

00:13:15.090 --> 00:13:19.340
Mami-kun, we've been fighting your
disease to the best of our ability.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:22.610
We need you to hold on to hope,
and fight with us!

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.820
It's pointless! Even in my dreams,

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:27.050
I see the Grim Reaper!

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:29.030
He's not the Grim Reaper.

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:32.210
He's a patient from another
ward of the hospital.

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:33.250
That's a lie!

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:35.180
No human could look like that!

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:37.050
He's not human.

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:40.060
He's some creature from the dark beyond!

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:43.580
A creature from the dark beyond...

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:45.850
What an intuitive girl.

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:49.150
That intuition could be how she 
was able to realize she was ill,

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:53.390
as well as what's causing her 
to fear death more than most.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:58.620
But if he's begun to wander the hospital 
at night, it's going to be a problem.

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:01.210
He's probably afraid of going to sleep...

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:03.530
Actually, sir, what's the status of that man?

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:04.850
That patient?

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:07.140
He should be waking up soon.

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:09.070
Let's check in on him.

00:14:09.730 --> 00:14:13.830
I don't really know much about his case, sir.

00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:16.290
Could you fill me in?

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.040
I hear he has unusual dreams?

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:21.520
I suppose you haven't
been here for that long.

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:23.750
His name is Mukouda Tetsurou.

00:14:23.980 --> 00:14:27.290
He came to the hospital two months ago,

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:31.220
saying he was suffering from long dreams.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:32.400
Long dreams?

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:35.050
How long do they feel?

00:14:35.050 --> 00:14:36.590
In the beginning,

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:40.600
which was about a month ago...

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:45.990
A single night's dream felt like
it lasted two or three days.

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:51.870
You're saying they feel long after waking up?

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:52.570
No...

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:55.250
The length of the dreams
themselves feels long.

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:57.760
At first I thought I was just imagining it,

00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:00.850
but with each day,
they get increasingly longer...

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:03.570
Which would be fine if 
they were all good dreams,

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:06.800
but there are lots of nightmares, too,
so it's starting to make me really anxious.

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:10.160
How long of a time span
do you dream of, currently?

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:12.980
Last night's dream lasted about a year.

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:14.360
Oh, a whole year?

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:16.310
Doctor, I'm serious!

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:19.110
It's getting harder to discern 
dreams from reality,

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:21.690
and it's begun to negatively impact my life.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:26.820
Think about it... For me, 
yesterday was a year ago.

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:33.280
<i>I decided to start by admitting him
and monitoring his sleep cycle.</i>

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:31.910
<b>General Hospital</b>

00:15:34.310 --> 00:15:36.210
<i>And that night...</i>

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:47.090
<i>Convulsions all over his body 
and rapid eye movement...</i>

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:50.180
<i>But it ended in an instant.</i>

00:15:50.180 --> 00:15:54.890
<i>His brain activity indicated he was in the 
deepest phase of sleep at that moment.</i>

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:56.850
Hey! Listen to me! Wake up!

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:03.010
Were you dreaming?!

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:07.060
Where am I?

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:08.690
This is the hospital.

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:10.990
You were admitted yesterday.

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:13.810
Admitted...

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:17.230
Oh, I remember now.

00:16:17.230 --> 00:16:19.230
I checked into the hospital...

00:16:19.230 --> 00:16:21.080
Yes, I was dreaming.

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:23.600
It was a terrifying one.

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:26.190
And it lasted a year and a half.

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:30.760
<i>My instincts told me this man was not lying,</i>

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:35.720
<i>and he truly was suffering from long dreams.</i>

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:40.970
Doctor, when will I be cured?

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:42.990
I have a few potential treatments in mind,

00:16:42.990 --> 00:16:44.730
but I need you to be patient for now.

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:48.000
Last night's dream lasted ten years...

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:50.160
They keep getting longer.

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:52.150
Listen to me, Mukouda-kun.

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:53.840
What you're experiencing is an illusion.

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:56.020
It was really only a few moments.

00:16:56.020 --> 00:16:58.890
You don't need to fear
the length of these dreams.

00:16:58.890 --> 00:17:03.620
You're only saying that because you've
never had one of my dreams, Doctor.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:07.160
You don't know how realistic they feel...

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:10.490
How disturbing and how lonely they are.

00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:12.990
How frightening they are...

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:15.710
Yes, but it's all in your mind.

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:19.230
We're working hard to find
the cause of your dreams.

00:17:19.230 --> 00:17:20.560
Please hurry!

00:17:21.210 --> 00:17:23.870
Otherwise, I get the feeling my
dreams are going to last a hundred,

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:26.020
and eventually two hundred, years.

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:28.380
If that happens...

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:30.560
I think I'll lose my mind.

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:32.260
And as he predicted,

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:36.150
the length of his dreams seemed 
to increase exponentially over time.

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:39.340
In time that became obvious, even to us.

00:17:39.340 --> 00:17:43.600
It was like we were watching
the evolution of mankind unfold...

00:17:47.090 --> 00:17:49.250
Are you awake, Mukouda-kun?

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:55.090
Where am I?

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:56.770
Who are you people?

00:17:56.770 --> 00:17:59.160
I'm your doctor, Kuroda.

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:00.140
Try to remember.

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:03.730
No!

00:18:03.730 --> 00:18:08.140
Lately, when he wakes up,
he tends to do bizarre things like this.

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:11.440
Do you suppose he still
thinks he's dreaming?

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:13.730
Where is Mami?

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:15.880
My wife Mami isn't here!

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:19.290
That's right, this is the hospital
where I first met her!

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:20.510
Mami!

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:22.120
Where is Mami?!

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:25.080
Mami-chan, you have to eat.

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:26.730
I don't want to.

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:29.100
Ugh, the idea of dying...

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:30.990
Mami!

00:18:30.990 --> 00:18:33.200
No!

00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:34.580
Mami!

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:38.800
You've come for me again, Reaper!

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:40.240
That's quite enough!

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:42.010
You need to go back to your room!

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:42.000
Reaper?

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:44.180
She called me the Reaper?

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:45.410
That's right...

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:47.030
I was dreaming.

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:51.090
Dr. Kuroda, I'm frightened.

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:54.190
If my dreams keep getting longer...

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:57.730
I can't help but wonder if it'll ever end.

00:18:57.730 --> 00:19:02.110
What will become of me if 
I dream an endless dream?

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:05.620
What will happen to me?

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:09.510
I'm so scared!

00:19:09.510 --> 00:19:11.010
Mami-chan!

00:19:09.510 --> 00:19:12.290
I don't wanna die!

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:14.510
It's okay! Calm down.

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:15.490
I don't wanna die!

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:22.230
I've never seen any patient with
such an intense fear of death before.

00:19:22.230 --> 00:19:24.300
What about Mukouda Tetsurou?

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:29.930
I can't begin to imagine how far
into the future he's dreamed now...

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:22.800
<i>As I watched the husk
of his remains blow away,</i>

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:27.300
<i>I wondered if his mind had
vanished into an unending dream.</i>

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:33.820
<i>I discovered an unidentified,</i>

00:20:33.820 --> 00:20:37.340
<i>crystallized material within
the remains of his brain.</i>

00:20:37.890 --> 00:20:44.470
<i>I suspected it had something
to do with his unusual dreams.</i>

00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:49.800
How are you feeling, Mami-kun?

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:52.140
Dr. Kuroda...

00:20:52.590 --> 00:20:55.460
I'm feeling pretty good lately.

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:56.780
I see.

00:20:57.620 --> 00:21:00.990
But, Doctor... One thing is odd.

00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:04.630
My dreams seem so long lately...

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:10.990
Sir,

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:14.330
have you noticed the changes in 
Takeshima Mami's condition lately?

00:21:14.720 --> 00:21:17.680
Her appearance is beginning
to change, too.

00:21:17.680 --> 00:21:19.760
She's looking like him...

00:21:19.760 --> 00:21:21.220
What do you suppose happened?

00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:27.630
I've been administering the crystals
I retrieved from Mukouda Tetsurou to her.

00:21:27.630 --> 00:21:29.260
Wh-What?!

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:31.670
She was afraid of dying.

00:21:31.670 --> 00:21:35.050
Afraid more than anything else
of her existence coming to an end.

00:21:35.050 --> 00:21:38.740
But what would happen if she
could dream an eternal dream?

00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:43.000
It would amount to her mind never dying.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:46.440
Even if it was, in reality,
a momentary illusion.

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:53.500
And if humanity were able to obtain
the means of dreaming endless dreams,

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:59.000
we would be able to permanently
rid ourselves of the fear of death.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
Collection
